# Build trees: anchored to the root, directories only. The old `*build*`
# matched any file with "build" in its name anywhere (e.g.
# docs/building-test.md), silently never committing it.
/build*/
/Testing*/
# Vestigial since #27 (version.hpp is generated into the build tree now), but
# kept: checkouts that predate it still have a stale generated file on disk.
include/version.hpp

# Prerequisites
*.d

# Compiled Object files
*.slo
*.lo
*.o
*.obj

# Precompiled Headers
*.gch
*.pch

# Compiled Dynamic libraries
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll

# Fortran module files
*.mod
*.smod

# Compiled Static libraries
*.lai
*.la
*.a
*.lib

# Executables
*.exe
*.out
*.app

# Core dumps. Deliberately crashing a test binary is a normal part of
# verifying a [uaf] case (revert the fix, confirm it segfaults), and the
# dump lands in the repo root — a 10MB blob one `git add -A` away from
# history. Anchored: an unanchored `core` also matches every *directory*
# named core (src/lib/core/, include/termforge/core/), which blocks
# `git add` of tracked files inside them.
/core
/core.*

# editor
*.swp
*.swo

# screenshots / local artifacts
remmina_*.png
*.png.local
